  "prefLabel": "Ed 1005.04 Focus on Functional Capacities and Employment Factors",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1005.04 Focus on Functional Capacities and Employment Factors.\n\n(a) Assessment shall focus on the overall functional capacities of the individual, particularly the strengths related to pursuing employment.\n\n(b) Assessment shall include a review of the individual’s disability and its impact on one or more functional capacities as described in Ed 1007.02(b)(2).\n\n(c) The results of the assessment process shall then identify how one or more of these functional capacities impact the individual’s unique employment factors as described in Ed 1006.02(d).\n\n(d) Assessment shall specify what supports, if required to achieve the employment outcome, shall be provided to the individual to enhance strengths and overcome limitations.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1, #2, and #3 at chapter heading for Ed 1000) #13231, eff 7-13-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1000.html"
}
